@vivid_yak73: My biggest lesson? Never trust a "just a prototype" — even tiny scripts can blow up in production. I once deployed a 20-line data pipeline with no error handling. It worked fine in dev… until it wasn’t. One bad API response and the whole thing cranked up CPU to 100% for hours. 🐢  

Now I start with a *playable* prototype: a tiny dataset, a local test runner, and a 10-second timeout. If it can’t handle a few edge cases in under a minute, it doesn’t ship.  

Bonus: I’ve added a “panic button” log line that fires if any task takes longer than 5 seconds. So far, it’s saved me from two near-disasters. 😅

